        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12401320/comment/12839860",
          "id": "12839860",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=monkiki",
            "name": "monkiki",
            "key": "monkiki",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Paco Avila",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Madrid"
          },
          "body": "The GQL.execute() returns a RowIterator and would be nice to return a QueryResult, so I can make a result.getColumnNames() to get the returned column names. Or perhaps better, make public the method which translates the GQL query to XPath so I can pass it to the QueryManager and execute it.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=monkiki",
            "name": "monkiki",
            "key": "monkiki",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Paco Avila",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Madrid"
          },
          "created": "2010-03-01T21:17:59.435+0000",
          "updated": "2010-03-01T21:17:59.435+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12401320/comment/12839864",
          "id": "12839864",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=monkiki",
            "name": "monkiki",
            "key": "monkiki",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Paco Avila",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Madrid"
          },
          "body": "Another option is to handle these kind of queries internally making possible to run it as:\n\nqueryManager.createQuery(statement, type);\n\nWhere \"type\" could be \"gql\" in this case, and the statement a GQL query.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=monkiki",
            "name": "monkiki",
            "key": "monkiki",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Paco Avila",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Madrid"
          },
          "created": "2010-03-01T21:20:04.564+0000",
          "updated": "2010-03-01T21:20:04.564+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12401320/comment/12839877",
          "id": "12839877",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=eclesia",
            "name": "eclesia",
            "key": "eclesia",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "johann sorel",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "\"GQL\" has no relation with JCR. it is just a candidate amoung several others  (like Common Query Language or Contextual Query Language) to write a query.\nSee : http://www.loc.gov/standards/sru/specs/cql.html\n\nCQL and GQL are not part of the JCR, and having the \"Google\" name in it does give it any rights to live in the JCR common module.\nIf you need another query language I suggest you add it in a different module,\nthis way you won't force everyone to have it if they don't want it.\n\nSome of my projects rely on the jcr-commun module and  I hope it will remain dedicated to \"pure\" JCR.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=eclesia",
            "name": "eclesia",
            "key": "eclesia",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "johann sorel",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2010-03-01T21:52:48.114+0000",
          "updated": "2010-03-01T21:52:48.114+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12401320/comment/12840064",
          "id": "12840064",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=monkiki",
            "name": "monkiki",
            "key": "monkiki",
            "avatarUrls": {
